        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Who repairs NordicTrack treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Under warranty, iFIT, NordicTrack's parent company, preauthorises the repair and sends parts or one of its authorised service providers; you start the request at my.iFIT.com. Out of warranty you can still go through iFIT, hire an independent fitness equipment technician, or fit the part yourself.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I get my NordicTrack treadmill fixed under warranty?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Go to my.iFIT.com with the model and serial number from the silver decal near the bottom of the frame, describe the fault and attach a short video if you can. iFIT must preauthorise warranty repairs, and may ship a part or send a technician. The manual warns of a possible minimal handling or trip charge.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the warranty on a NordicTrack treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It varies by model, and the terms in your manual are the ones that apply. The current X24 manual gives a lifetime drive motor for the original purchaser, 10 years on the frame, 2 years on parts and 1 year on the tablet and labour (checked November 2026). Some T Series pages describe a shorter motor warranty.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much does it cost to repair a NordicTrack treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Our general estimates: a call-out fee around $75 to $150, simple jobs such as a drive belt or speed sensor $120 to $300 all in, and a motor control board or drive motor with a technician commonly $300 to $900. Touchscreen consoles and larger models sit at the top of the range. Under warranty, covered parts and labour are free apart from any handling or trip charge.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where can I buy NordicTrack treadmill parts?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              NordicTrack manuals send parts orders to iFIT customer service: quote the model number, serial number, product name and the key number of the part from the manual's parts list. Independent sellers such as FitnessRepairParts and Sears PartsDirect also list NordicTrack parts by model number, which helps for older machines.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the NordicTrack warranty transferable if I buy used?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. The X24 manual says the warranty extends only to the original purchaser and is not transferable. A second-hand NordicTrack is repaired at the owner's cost, so factor that into the price you pay and into any repair-or-replace decision.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is it worth repairing an old NordicTrack treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Usually yes when the frame and deck are sound and one part has failed, especially on a Commercial or X-series model. Usually no when the quote nears the price of a new entry model, several parts are worn, or the part is no longer available for your model number.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
          <div class="author-card">
            <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="56" height="56" loading="lazy" />
            <div>
              <div class="ac-k">Written by</div>
